1
00:00:19,840 --> 00:00:24,280
Anyone who's broke, come to my place.

2
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:29,040
I'm broke too, but don't worry.

3
00:00:29,040 --> 00:00:36,320
Look, blue skies and white clouds.

4
00:00:37,880 --> 00:00:42,680
Things will work out somehow, eventually.

5
00:00:44,760 --> 00:00:45,980
You get it, right?

6
00:00:45,980 --> 00:00:47,980
I get it, I get it.

7
00:00:47,980 --> 00:00:51,980
Once you understand, shut up and follow me.

8
00:01:05,240 --> 00:01:09,380
Man, this summer was a strange one.

9
00:01:10,580 --> 00:01:11,620
Whoa, everything...

10
00:01:11,620 --> 00:01:13,600
Bro, you suck at this.

11
00:01:21,980 --> 00:01:22,080
Mm.

12
00:01:23,800 --> 00:01:24,200
Mm.

13
00:01:26,100 --> 00:01:26,500
Mm.

14
00:01:27,480 --> 00:01:27,880
Mm.

15
00:01:29,620 --> 00:01:31,880
If it's about love, what would you do?

16
00:01:32,280 --> 00:01:32,680
Me.

17
00:01:33,560 --> 00:01:33,960
Me.

18
00:01:37,660 --> 00:01:42,940
He climbed up but can't get back down, I guess.
Can't be helped, I'll go.

19
00:01:42,940 --> 00:01:43,680
Me.

20
00:01:55,300 --> 00:01:56,580
Are you okay, old man?

21
00:02:02,080 --> 00:02:05,680
Listen, we're going down one step at a time,
nice and slow.

22
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:14,360
Eeeeeeee

23
00:02:14,360 --> 00:02:15,600
Eeeeeeee

24
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:22,860
Hold on tight.

25
00:02:25,120 --> 00:02:26,860
Don't let go, you hear?

26
00:02:26,860 --> 00:02:29,120
Aaaaaaaa

27
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:52,520
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu

28
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:57,220
I heard you also climbed up onto the roofs of the Kannon Hall and the five-story pagoda in Asakusa,
didn't you?

29
00:02:57,220 --> 00:03:01,140
Taito, Sumida, and Katsushika wards,
fourteen houses in total.

30
00:03:01,140 --> 00:03:04,040
Plus this time, the chimney at Kameno-yu,

31
00:03:04,040 --> 00:03:06,320
Are you a habitual offender or what?

32
00:03:08,500 --> 00:03:09,220
Go ahead.

33
00:03:09,220 --> 00:03:10,020
Thank you.

34
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,760
If you like high places,

35
00:03:13,760 --> 00:03:17,460
there are plenty of safer,
easier places to climb, surely.

36
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:19,440
Safe?

37
00:03:19,440 --> 00:03:19,620
Safe?

38
00:03:20,160 --> 00:03:25,860
There's some tower, department store rooftops,
tall buildings everywhere in Tokyo.

39
00:03:26,380 --> 00:03:30,340
At your age, you don't have to struggle up
a bathhouse chimney or anything like that.

40
00:03:30,340 --> 00:03:32,700
Well, new places are just not my thing.

41
00:03:32,700 --> 00:03:35,200
New or old, it doesn't matter.

42
00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:37,920
I'm telling you not to bother other people.

43
00:03:39,180 --> 00:03:40,440
Did I bother anyone?

44
00:03:41,040 --> 00:03:45,040
You did!
The bathhouse, me, and the neighbors!

45
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:48,320
I see. That was wrong of me.

46
00:03:50,680 --> 00:03:51,400
Is that all?

47
00:03:52,160 --> 00:03:55,460
Why don't you let him off for today,
Ryo-chan?

48
00:03:55,980 --> 00:03:56,710
Got it?

49
00:03:56,760 --> 00:04:00,040
Don't you dare climb up again.
I won't save you next time.

50
00:04:00,040 --> 00:04:03,040
Yes, thank you for all your help.

51
00:04:06,220 --> 00:04:09,480
Apparently that old man
has no family or relatives.

52
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:18,000
Just then, a warm breeze went pyororororo.

53
00:04:19,440 --> 00:04:21,000
Ameshii.

54
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:23,280
Stop it already, Ryo-san.

55
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:47,900
!

56
00:04:47,900 --> 00:04:48,420
Ugh.

57
00:04:52,240 --> 00:04:52,900
Nooo...

58
00:04:59,240 --> 00:05:01,260
So the cops finally showed up

59
00:05:03,160 --> 00:05:08,960
I figured spreading ghost rumors about this rundown
temple would keep people away and make it safe.

60
00:05:10,900 --> 00:05:12,300
What are you doing there?

61
00:05:13,860 --> 00:05:14,620
Stop right there!

62
00:05:20,900 --> 00:05:22,040
Come quietly.

63
00:05:22,700 --> 00:05:23,580
Ryo-san

64
00:05:26,240 --> 00:05:26,800
Terai

65
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:28,760
Are you all right, Ryo-san?

66
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:33,280
Terai, take care of this guy.

67
00:05:33,780 --> 00:05:35,820
That over there is probably stolen goods.

68
00:05:35,820 --> 00:05:38,200
There are still a few more inside.

69
00:05:38,680 --> 00:05:39,620
Yeah, got it.

70
00:05:40,060 --> 00:05:41,220
And Ryo-san?

71
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:44,420
I'll handle the cleanup for this one.

72
00:05:49,880 --> 00:05:51,120
Is that all of it?

73
00:05:54,320 --> 00:05:57,460
It's a delinquent's accident,
so don't hold it against us.

74
00:05:57,460 --> 00:05:58,760
How many?

75
00:06:01,260 --> 00:06:01,740
Alright.

76
00:06:19,720 --> 00:06:20,840
Excuse me

77
00:06:20,840 --> 00:06:23,260
Yes, yes, what is it?

78
00:06:23,260 --> 00:06:23,980
Hello

79
00:06:25,900 --> 00:06:27,680
I'm lost,

80
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:29,260
where are you trying to go?

81
00:06:31,040 --> 00:06:31,920
Asakusa.

82
00:06:31,920 --> 00:06:33,220
Asakusa?

83
00:06:33,920 --> 00:06:35,320
Yes, Asakusa.

84
00:06:36,180 --> 00:06:40,540
Well, first,
take a left at the shopping street up ahead,

85
00:06:40,540 --> 00:06:42,160
and you'll reach Kameari Station.

86
00:06:42,160 --> 00:06:45,140
From there,
take the Joban Line to Kita-Senju,

87
00:06:45,140 --> 00:06:49,080
then transfer to the Tobu Isesaki Line,
and the last stop is Asakusa.

88
00:06:49,080 --> 00:06:50,120
Got it?

89
00:06:51,700 --> 00:06:54,920
From Kameari Station,
take the Joban Line to Kita-Senju,

90
00:06:54,920 --> 00:06:57,980
then take the Tobu Isesaki
Line to the final stop.

91
00:06:58,860 --> 00:07:00,200
Yes, thank you very much.

92
00:07:06,360 --> 00:07:06,800
What is it?

93
00:07:12,160 --> 00:07:15,960
Shokichi-san! Climbing up somewhere like that again,
isn't it dangerous!

94
00:07:16,100 --> 00:07:17,800
Come down quickly!

95
00:07:18,420 --> 00:07:19,560
It's fine, it's fine.

96
00:07:20,260 --> 00:07:24,300
That's not okay! If you don't come down,
we'll come up to get you! Understood?

97
00:07:29,720 --> 00:07:30,900
What is it, what happened?

98
00:07:33,260 --> 00:07:34,800
I couldn't find the station.

99
00:07:35,440 --> 00:07:37,425
It's been over an hour since then, you know.

100
00:07:37,475 --> 00:07:40,020
It's not even a road where you'd get lost,
you know.

101
00:07:41,560 --> 00:07:46,740
Alright, alright. Once you've finished eating,
I'll drive you there in an Ejima cab, so just wait a bit.

102
00:07:47,500 --> 00:07:48,660
Yes, I'll wait.

103
00:07:57,840 --> 00:08:01,800
Stop staring at me like that, it makes it hard to eat.
Are you hungry or something?

104
00:08:04,280 --> 00:08:05,320
What's your name?

105
00:08:05,720 --> 00:08:06,620
It's Hanayo.

106
00:08:08,960 --> 00:08:11,240
Anyway, how old are you?

107
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:12,740
Seventeen.

108
00:08:14,960 --> 00:08:16,420
Where did you come from?

109
00:08:17,380 --> 00:08:19,700
That way.

110
00:08:19,700 --> 00:08:21,160
"That way," you say?

111
00:08:21,720 --> 00:08:22,780
Over there.

112
00:08:22,780 --> 00:08:24,400
Don't make fun of the police.

113
00:08:29,780 --> 00:08:31,520
Morning, Ryo-chan.

114
00:08:31,520 --> 00:08:33,700
Reiko. Perfect timing.

115
00:08:33,700 --> 00:08:37,260
I'm taking this girl to the station,
so mind the place while I'm gone.

116
00:08:37,260 --> 00:08:38,640
This girl?

117
00:08:39,640 --> 00:08:41,720
I'll be right back. Let's go.

118
00:08:41,720 --> 00:08:42,260
Yes.

119
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:51,260
Long time no see, Asakusa.

120
00:08:51,260 --> 00:08:56,060
It's rare these days for a young girl
to go sightseeing in Asakusa alone.

121
00:08:56,060 --> 00:08:59,940
I'm not alone. I'm meeting a friend.

122
00:09:00,420 --> 00:09:04,940
What? Then just have your
friend come pick you up partway.

123
00:09:04,940 --> 00:09:07,780
Doesn't that friend have a cell phone?

124
00:09:08,580 --> 00:09:11,660
A cell phone? I don't think she has one.

125
00:09:12,140 --> 00:09:13,100
Rare

126
00:09:13,680 --> 00:09:17,860
Though I don't think it's right for
every student nowadays to have one either.

127
00:09:19,120 --> 00:09:23,420
You're not a runaway girl, are you?

128
00:09:23,420 --> 00:09:24,620
N-no, I'm not.

129
00:09:24,620 --> 00:09:27,440
Really? Then where's your home?

130
00:09:27,440 --> 00:09:29,520
"Over there" or "over here" won't do.

131
00:09:29,520 --> 00:09:31,460
Tell me your address. Your address.

132
00:09:34,480 --> 00:09:35,640
Here?

133
00:09:36,200 --> 00:09:40,360
So that means you can't
possibly be a temple's daughter.

134
00:09:40,360 --> 00:09:43,160
There's no head priest at this temple,
you know.

135
00:09:43,160 --> 00:09:45,600
So what that means is, you're lying.

136
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:47,500
Huh?

137
00:09:48,640 --> 00:09:49,900
Hanayo's gone.

138
00:09:55,600 --> 00:10:00,160
Hanayo, if you're going to mess around, I'm going home.
You understand?

139
00:10:00,740 --> 00:10:01,520
Ryo-san

140
00:10:02,280 --> 00:10:03,460
Since when?

141
00:10:03,460 --> 00:10:08,680
Ryo-san,
you'll take Hanayo to Asakusa, right?

142
00:10:08,680 --> 00:10:11,800
No. I can't help a liar.

143
00:10:13,020 --> 00:10:16,080
I thought I put everything back yesterday.

144
00:10:16,880 --> 00:10:20,000
Ryo-san, you left one thing
behind when you went home.

145
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:21,940
Why would you know that?

146
00:10:22,840 --> 00:10:26,420
If I tell the truth,
will you take me to Asakusa?

147
00:10:31,140 --> 00:10:33,740
Su-sam, what do you mean by the truth?

148
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:36,980
Where I came from.

149
00:10:40,520 --> 00:10:44,180
It's like something came out from under
the grave I knocked over while apologizing.

150
00:10:46,080 --> 00:10:47,580
Those meaningful glances are too much.

151
00:10:51,960 --> 00:10:53,100
Now that you mention it,

152
00:10:53,100 --> 00:10:56,860
I've got a few things to think about,
one, two, three, four, five.

153
00:10:59,740 --> 00:11:00,920
Don't run away, Ryo-san.

154
00:11:01,580 --> 00:11:02,360
Got it.

155
00:11:02,360 --> 00:11:03,780
I'll wake him up right away.

156
00:11:04,320 --> 00:11:05,240
Here we go.

157
00:11:05,240 --> 00:11:06,720
There, I've woken him up.

158
00:11:10,860 --> 00:11:12,540
Why won't it go away?

159
00:11:17,080 --> 00:11:19,300
I'm sorry for knocking over the grave.

160
00:11:19,300 --> 00:11:21,900
Please return and rest in peace.

161
00:11:22,760 --> 00:11:25,460
What more do you want me to do?

162
00:11:26,820 --> 00:11:29,200
I really want to go to Asakusa.

163
00:11:29,200 --> 00:11:31,740
Ryo-san, please take me there.

164
00:11:31,740 --> 00:11:33,700
It's me who wants to pray to you.

165
00:11:39,060 --> 00:11:40,880
Trampled right beneath the eyes

166
00:11:42,440 --> 00:11:43,320
Visible

167
00:11:43,920 --> 00:11:45,080
Not visible

168
00:11:45,740 --> 00:11:46,620
Visible

169
00:11:47,340 --> 00:11:48,480
Not visible

170
00:11:48,480 --> 00:11:51,880
So you can only be seen by me, is that it?

171
00:11:54,560 --> 00:11:55,700
Ryo-san

172
00:11:58,960 --> 00:12:01,560
I feel guilty,
like we're riding without paying.

173
00:12:06,280 --> 00:12:07,600
We're here, Hana.

174
00:12:07,600 --> 00:12:09,280
This is Asakusa.

175
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:17,340
This is Asakusa?

176
00:12:18,720 --> 00:12:20,920
And this is the Asakusa Rokku.

177
00:12:22,180 --> 00:12:24,420
Movie theaters and playhouses
are concentrated here.

178
00:12:24,420 --> 00:12:27,160
It used to be a bit livelier, though.

179
00:12:28,280 --> 00:12:29,000
Here?

180
00:12:30,160 --> 00:12:32,300
There's somewhere I want to go, too.

181
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:33,260
Is that all right?

182
00:12:39,280 --> 00:12:40,840
Give me some amulets and talismans.

183
00:12:40,840 --> 00:12:42,240
There are various kinds, though.

184
00:12:42,240 --> 00:12:43,880
The whole set, all of them.

185
00:12:48,620 --> 00:12:49,840
Not good enough?

186
00:12:49,840 --> 00:12:53,520
Thanks to you, it's cool and I'm saved.

187
00:12:53,520 --> 00:12:58,160
Now that you mention it,
you said earlier you were meeting someone.

188
00:12:58,160 --> 00:13:02,240
I promised Masakichi-san we'd
climb up to the 12th floor together.

189
00:13:02,900 --> 00:13:05,720
The 12th floor? Which building's 12th floor?

190
00:13:06,280 --> 00:13:07,320
Asakusa's.

191
00:13:09,280 --> 00:13:11,500
But there are fifty thousand
buildings with more than 12 floors!

192
00:13:11,500 --> 00:13:13,440
Are you planning to make
us climb every one of them?

193
00:13:16,060 --> 00:13:17,400
No way, seriously?

194
00:13:22,460 --> 00:13:23,600
I'm home.

195
00:13:23,600 --> 00:13:24,600
Ryo-chan.

196
00:13:24,600 --> 00:13:25,920
What happened to your face?

197
00:13:25,920 --> 00:13:27,180
What's wrong?

198
00:13:28,440 --> 00:13:30,100
You look awful.

199
00:13:30,560 --> 00:13:32,100
What on earth happened?

200
00:13:32,560 --> 00:13:34,480
They said Ryo-san was acting strange,

201
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:37,380
and Reiko was really worried about you.

202
00:13:39,280 --> 00:13:44,560
Yeah, yeah, just let me rest a bit.
I'm exhausted.

203
00:13:45,520 --> 00:13:47,560
Who are you talking to, Ryo-chan?

204
00:13:47,560 --> 00:13:49,380
Do you see something?

205
00:13:51,240 --> 00:13:52,520
It's Hanayo

206
00:13:53,040 --> 00:13:53,800
Hanayo?

207
00:13:53,800 --> 00:13:59,920
Last night, when I caught Akisu,
I took down that temple destroyer, remember?

208
00:14:00,400 --> 00:14:02,980
Looks like she followed me back from that.

209
00:14:05,080 --> 00:14:06,100
You're joking, right?

210
00:14:06,920 --> 00:14:09,400
Are you talking about a ghost?

211
00:14:09,800 --> 00:14:12,040
She's right in front of you all now.

212
00:14:12,040 --> 00:14:16,220
Dodging me like that? How rude.

213
00:14:17,080 --> 00:14:20,140
It can't be helped! Only I can see Hanayo.

214
00:14:20,140 --> 00:14:23,900
Anyone would be scared if they were
told something invisible was there.

215
00:14:26,220 --> 00:14:28,720
Apparently her maiden's heart is wounded.

216
00:14:28,720 --> 00:14:30,940
Is Hanayo-san a maiden?

217
00:14:30,940 --> 00:14:32,700
She's seventeen, apparently.

218
00:14:33,260 --> 00:14:35,620
I'm sorry for running away like that.

219
00:14:36,100 --> 00:14:38,720
I didn't mean any harm, it's just...

220
00:14:38,720 --> 00:14:41,500
I'm just not used to customers like you

221
00:14:43,720 --> 00:14:46,620
Hey, do you understand?

222
00:14:51,040 --> 00:14:53,100
Ryo-chan, are you all right?

223
00:14:53,460 --> 00:14:54,720
You look really pale.

224
00:14:55,340 --> 00:15:00,140
Yeah, until I fulfill Hanayo's lingering
wish and send her on to rest in peace,

225
00:15:00,140 --> 00:15:02,920
apparently she won't leave my side.

226
00:15:03,460 --> 00:15:05,800
I wonder if Ryo-chan's body
can hold out until then.

227
00:15:05,800 --> 00:15:09,860
What is Senpai Hanayo's
lingering wish, anyway?

228
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:15,720
She wants to climb to the twelfth
floor of a building in Asakusa.

229
00:15:15,720 --> 00:15:19,480
I tried climbing every
12-story building I could see,

230
00:15:19,960 --> 00:15:21,900
but apparently none of
them are the right one.

231
00:15:23,380 --> 00:15:24,180
Twelve stories.

232
00:15:25,560 --> 00:15:30,280
She promised her boyfriend Masakichi
that they'd go to that place together,

233
00:15:30,280 --> 00:15:32,600
but it seems she never
got to keep that promise.

234
00:15:33,040 --> 00:15:34,820
So that was her regret.

235
00:15:34,820 --> 00:15:36,500
Masakichi?

236
00:15:36,820 --> 00:15:37,634
Ryo-san,

237
00:15:37,684 --> 00:15:41,000
the old man who likes high
places is also named Masakichi.

238
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:45,400
That Masakichi also wants to climb up high,
just like Hanayo-chan.

239
00:15:46,140 --> 00:15:48,980
Hey, hey, he's Hanayo's boyfriend!

240
00:15:48,980 --> 00:15:51,400
There's way too big an age difference!

241
00:15:52,160 --> 00:15:54,500
But it's too much of a
coincidence to be chance.

242
00:15:54,500 --> 00:15:55,160
Yeah.

243
00:15:56,180 --> 00:15:58,460
Hanayo, how old is Masakichi?

244
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:00,920
Two years older?

245
00:16:02,920 --> 00:16:04,300
Nineteen or twenty, I'd say.

246
00:16:04,940 --> 00:16:07,660
Unfortunately, no matter how you look at it,
they're different people.

247
00:16:07,660 --> 00:16:08,640
This is it.

248
00:16:09,140 --> 00:16:12,360
The twelve-story building Hanayo-san
talked about must be this one.

249
00:16:13,420 --> 00:16:14,540
Ryōunkaku

250
00:16:15,020 --> 00:16:17,660
Commonly known as the
Asakusa Twelve Stories.

251
00:16:18,260 --> 00:16:22,980
In 1890,
a twelve-story brick tower rose in Asakusa.

252
00:16:22,980 --> 00:16:25,200
Ryōunkaku opened.

253
00:16:25,760 --> 00:16:28,360
The view from the observation
deck was exceptional,

254
00:16:28,360 --> 00:16:30,880
with Mount Fuji and Tsukuba
visible above the clouds.

255
00:16:30,880 --> 00:16:36,020
On clear days, it was said you could see as
far as Hakone and Nikkō through a telescope.

256
00:16:36,020 --> 00:16:42,340
In its early days, sightseers paying the
admission fee to climb up were endless.

257
00:16:45,220 --> 00:16:51,560
On September 1, 1923, the Great Kantō Earthquake
snapped it off at the eighth floor, and it was lost.

258
00:16:52,300 --> 00:16:56,940
That same month it was blown up,
and the twelfth floor vanished from Asakusa.

259
00:16:57,562 --> 00:17:03,160
No wonder it was gone before I was born.

260
00:17:03,920 --> 00:17:07,740
If we trace Masakichi's
age back to Hanayo's age,

261
00:17:07,740 --> 00:17:09,820
it would be roughly the late Taishō era.

262
00:17:09,820 --> 00:17:13,380
Could Hanayo have died
in the earthquake too?

263
00:17:19,900 --> 00:17:23,280
Hanayo:
Give up on the twelve-story building.

264
00:17:23,280 --> 00:17:25,500
You can't climb something that doesn't exist,
after all.

265
00:17:27,320 --> 00:17:45,300
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

266
00:17:45,300 --> 00:17:47,200
Ken-chan, Masakichi-san...

267
00:17:47,200 --> 00:17:50,880
That's because Masakichi-san
is nowhere to be found.

268
00:17:52,820 --> 00:17:55,780
Please, find old man Masakichi!

269
00:17:55,780 --> 00:17:56,500
Understood.

270
00:17:57,080 --> 00:17:59,280
Let's ask Honda and the
others for backup too.

271
00:18:00,040 --> 00:18:02,800
Search every high place thoroughly.

272
00:18:05,940 --> 00:18:08,140
I gave him a pretty
stern warning this morning,

273
00:18:08,140 --> 00:18:12,240
so I don't think he'll be climbing
up high places for a while.

274
00:18:12,660 --> 00:18:14,080
Why would you do that?

275
00:18:15,300 --> 00:18:17,680
"Be kind to me,"
that's what I've always told you.

276
00:18:17,680 --> 00:18:19,900
But as you were leaving, Ryo-san said

277
00:18:19,900 --> 00:18:22,120
"Don't spoil him, you hear me, Temple."

278
00:18:22,120 --> 00:18:25,820
If we don't put our foot down,
that old man will keep repeating himself.

279
00:18:26,980 --> 00:18:27,640
Ryo-san.

280
00:18:29,880 --> 00:18:32,658
We don't have time.
If searching is too difficult,

281
00:18:32,708 --> 00:18:34,300
then we have no choice but to lure him out.

282
00:18:34,300 --> 00:18:36,500
Lure him out? How?

283
00:18:37,260 --> 00:18:37,980
Nakagawa.

284
00:18:37,980 --> 00:18:38,600
Yes?

285
00:18:39,160 --> 00:18:41,355
With your power, once more,

286
00:18:41,405 --> 00:18:44,100
build the Ryōunkaku in Asakusa for me.

287
00:18:59,080 --> 00:19:01,420
No good, he's nowhere to be seen.

288
00:19:01,420 --> 00:19:02,420
This way's no good either.

289
00:19:02,860 --> 00:19:04,680
But we have to find the old man.

290
00:19:04,680 --> 00:19:06,300
What does it mean that
Ryotsu's life is in danger?

291
00:19:06,300 --> 00:19:07,460
What's that supposed to mean?

292
00:19:07,460 --> 00:19:08,500
I don't know.

293
00:19:10,100 --> 00:19:11,480
We're here, Ryo-san.

294
00:19:12,060 --> 00:19:12,640
Aaaaah!

295
00:19:12,640 --> 00:19:13,760
Aaaaah!

296
00:19:19,180 --> 00:19:27,200
Well, what's gotten into you?
Are you really Ryotsu?

297
00:19:27,200 --> 00:19:29,280
The crossing will be going through shortly.

298
00:19:34,120 --> 00:19:35,440
What is that?

299
00:19:40,440 --> 00:19:42,000
Hey! It looks just like the real thing!

300
00:19:43,020 --> 00:19:48,560
It's a full-scale model, made by a Nakagawa
Group company that specializes in movie sets.

301
00:19:55,260 --> 00:19:57,400
Road closed beyond this point.

302
00:19:57,900 --> 00:20:00,380
Thank you for your cooperation!

303
00:20:00,380 --> 00:20:02,000
Damn it! Are you kidding me?!

304
00:20:02,460 --> 00:20:05,400
If you don't want to get crushed,
you'd better wait.

305
00:20:08,560 --> 00:20:11,520
We can only keep the road
closed for twenty minutes.

306
00:20:29,440 --> 00:20:33,400
Here's the view from the
12th floor you wanted to see.

307
00:20:35,400 --> 00:20:38,680
The scenery has changed quite
a bit since your time, though.

308
00:20:38,680 --> 00:20:42,440
This is the best I can do.

309
00:20:44,740 --> 00:20:46,460
Where are you, old man?

310
00:20:46,980 --> 00:20:48,780
Hanayo's waiting for you!

311
00:20:54,800 --> 00:21:01,200
How nostalgic.

312
00:21:03,140 --> 00:21:04,200
Old man...

313
00:21:04,200 --> 00:21:05,840
You...

314
00:21:06,360 --> 00:21:08,240
Never mind about me.

315
00:21:08,240 --> 00:21:09,900
You know Hanayo, don't you?

316
00:21:10,680 --> 00:21:13,060
Ahhh, of course I know her!

317
00:21:13,060 --> 00:21:16,160
Hanayo is right here. Can't you see her?

318
00:21:16,160 --> 00:21:18,380
Hanayo...

319
00:21:18,380 --> 00:21:21,600
It's Masakichi,
the one you wanted to see, Hanayo!

320
00:21:22,360 --> 00:21:25,220
Why won't you show yourself?

321
00:21:25,220 --> 00:21:29,620
You've become an old geezer,
so you can't tell who I am, can't you?

322
00:21:41,640 --> 00:21:42,720
Masakichi.

323
00:21:44,700 --> 00:21:47,840
Hanayo, where have you been all this time?

324
00:21:48,780 --> 00:21:54,580
I've been waiting,
believing you'd find me someday, Masakichi.

325
00:21:55,500 --> 00:22:00,880
After I lost Hanayo and the Twelve-Story Tower was gone too,
I didn't know what to do.

326
00:22:01,580 --> 00:22:02,640
What did you do?

327
00:22:03,380 --> 00:22:07,160
The Kannon Hall and the five-story
pagoda survived the fire,

328
00:22:07,160 --> 00:22:12,360
so I thought maybe if I climbed them,
I'd find Hanayo.

329
00:22:12,360 --> 00:22:13,700
You climbed them?

330
00:22:14,060 --> 00:22:14,500
Yes.

331
00:22:14,960 --> 00:22:19,660
Shrine torii, cedar trees,
bathhouse chimneys...

332
00:22:19,660 --> 00:22:21,980
I climbed all sorts of things.

333
00:22:23,140 --> 00:22:25,240
I was down below the whole time.

334
00:22:25,800 --> 00:22:28,780
I was waiting for you down below, Masakichi.

335
00:22:30,080 --> 00:22:32,060
I'm sorry, Hanayo.

336
00:22:32,060 --> 00:22:32,840
No.

337
00:22:33,560 --> 00:22:36,260
And now we've even climbed
the Twelve-Story together.

338
00:22:37,160 --> 00:22:38,940
I have no regrets left.

339
00:22:44,240 --> 00:22:45,580
I'll be leaving soon.

340
00:22:53,220 --> 00:22:54,620
Eeeeeeh?

341
00:22:54,620 --> 00:23:00,460
Eeeeeeh?

342
00:23:03,100 --> 00:23:03,900
Ōtani

343
00:23:04,560 --> 00:23:06,620
So many people have gathered.

344
00:23:06,620 --> 00:23:08,500
I wonder what happened.

345
00:23:13,380 --> 00:23:13,780
Right.

346
00:23:17,980 --> 00:23:20,160
Where did you meet Hanayo?

347
00:23:24,040 --> 00:23:27,260
Hanayo was a waitress at the Rock café.

348
00:23:28,720 --> 00:23:32,800
You live in Asakusa and have never even been up the twelve-story tower?
What a strange guy.

349
00:23:32,800 --> 00:23:35,840
Alright, I'll take you there sometime.

350
00:23:37,220 --> 00:23:40,640
Hanayo was the cutest girl at Rock.

351
00:23:41,580 --> 00:23:44,220
Picking up girls You're quite the ladies' man,
old man!

352
00:23:44,220 --> 00:23:47,360
It took me a whole year to win over Hanayo.

353
00:23:47,360 --> 00:23:54,000
Sorry for keeping you waiting
so long for our first date.

354
00:24:17,360 --> 00:24:24,540
On this rainy afternoon,
I walked looking back.

355
00:24:24,540 --> 00:24:34,100
Led by the hand by Gaaja,
the strange feeling I had back then.

356
00:24:35,540 --> 00:24:45,220
So on the arcade's tiles,
I tried walking only on the black ones.

357
00:24:47,900 --> 00:24:53,480
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone forgets.

358
00:24:54,580 --> 00:25:00,960
Politicians with their self-important faces,
and aunties with blue eyeshadow too.

359
00:25:00,960 --> 00:25:06,520
Try turning at that corner.

360
00:25:07,560 --> 00:25:11,680
You can meet everyone, everyone.

361
00:25:14,200 --> 00:25:16,380
Over there, there's a wall.

362
00:25:17,700 --> 00:25:19,660
Well, surely there's a wall.

363
00:25:21,180 --> 00:25:24,960
Everyone, come on over to our town.

364
00:25:26,100 --> 00:25:26,500
Thank you.

365
00:25:29,720 --> 00:25:31,600
It's huge! Way too huge!

366
00:25:31,780 --> 00:25:35,040
A giant athletic contest with
a 100 million yen winner's prize?

367
00:25:35,040 --> 00:25:37,820
So it's an athletic course
held inside something enormous?

368
00:25:37,820 --> 00:25:40,200
But to pay back a 100 million yen debt...

369
00:25:42,580 --> 00:25:46,420
Next time: a giant athletic contest
with 100 million yen at stake.

370
00:25:46,420 --> 00:25:47,460
See you then.

